  'A Gothic Revival Episcopal chapel by the New York architect Charles C. Haight, consecrated by Bishop Doane in 1871. The sanctuary is 24 by 62 feet with a chancel wing of 16 by 24 feet; the walls are brick faced with fieldstone.',
