  'A gable-fronted church of red Potsdam sandstone, built in 1883 with an 85-foot tower. Its Italianate rectory of about 1900, on a sandstone foundation, is now the Colton Town Museum.',
  'Sandstone church and tower, the clapboard rectory beside it, and an 1880s iron urn and lamppost on the grounds. Interior and museum opening days not checked.',
